  - gme_load_atlas declared extern void gme_load_atlas(const char * file); in gme.h. Defined in vlk.h as void gme_load_atlas(const char * name) inside VLK_IMPL. Fine if gme.h included where implemented? But gme_load_atlas is defined after vlk_load_atlas? Actually in diff: static void vlk_load_atlas renamed to void gme_load_atlas. It is in vlk.h with VLK_IMPL. But gme.h implementation includes sfx, snd, tim, brd. It calls gme_load_atlas. Since gme.h defines it static? It extern in gme.h; when GME_IMPL included, implementation of gme.h includes itself? Let's inspect.

  Original gme.h now contains declaration and inline implementation guarded by GME_IMPL. If a source file defines GME_IMPL and includes gme.h, implementation inserted. It calls gme_load_atlas(name). gme_load_atlas defined elsewhere in vlk.h? In app likely puzzle-osx.m includes gme.h then vlk.h? Need know include ordering. gme.h declares extern gme_load_atlas. Implementation of gme.h at top includes brd, sfx, snd, tim, but not vlk.h. Calls gme_load_atlas. Link resolves to function in vlk.h compiled where VLK_IMPL. OK.

